Building PinglyMotion
==================

PinglyMotion is built with CMake and Qt 6. Running it needs
a graphics card and driver with OpenGL 3.3 or newer.

Linux (Debian/Ubuntu):

    sudo apt-get install cmake g++ qt6-base-dev qt6-base-dev-tools \
        libqt6opengl6-dev libgl-dev
    cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
    cmake --build build
    cd bin && ../build/src/PinglyMotion

Windows (MinGW from the Qt installer):

    cmake -S . -B build -G "MinGW Makefiles" -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
    cmake --build build

    Copy build/src/PinglyMotion.exe next to a copy of bin/data and run
    windeployqt on it. .github/workflows/build.yml shows the exact steps.

Add -DPINGLYMOTION_TESTS=ON to build the tests, then run
"ctest --test-dir build" (see README.md).

The program reads its data folder from next to the executable. A program
run from the build folder uses bin/data in the source tree.
